    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d605">

                <pb facs="0579" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg567"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6082: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-16T19:00:00+03:00">October 16, 1940—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1355. The press today publishes a Tass communiqué denying as “not in accordance
                    with the facts” a report stated to have appeared in the Danish newspaper under
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] <hi rendition="#italic">Politiken</hi>
                    from its Berlin correspondent to the effect that the Soviet Government was
                    informed “in due time that German forces were to be sent to Rumania and that the
                    Kremlin was informed as to the stand of these forces and as to the purposes for
                    which they were sent to Rumania.”<anchor n="36" xml:id="d605-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Repeated to Berlin and Bucharest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d605-f1" n="36" xml:id="d605-f1-content">
                <p>With regard to the presence of German troops in Rumania, see telegrams Nos. 579,
                    October 7, 6 p.m., and 585, October 9, 5 p.m., from the Minister in Rumania,
                        <ref target="#pg519">pp. 519</ref> and <ref target="#pg520">520</ref>,
                    respectively.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
